{"status":"success","data":[{"download":{"data":{"dataset":{"site":{"handle":"LA_SU-14","siteid":27196,"sitename":"Kopparas Mire","unittype":"Modern","geography":"{\"type\":\"Point\",\"crs\":{\"type\":\"name\",\"properties\":{\"name\":\"EPSG:4326\"}},\"coordinates\":[14.5381,57.1018]}","collectionunit":"SU-14","sitedescription":"Open peatland with scattered, small trees of Pinus sylvestris. The mire is weakly minerotrophic, but smaller spots are ombrotrophic. The water supplies are both soligenous and, to a lesser extent, topogenous. The mire surface slopes slightly (1: 164) towards the south-south west. The lawn vegetation of the area studied is dominated by Eriophorum angustifolium, Calluna vulgaris, Andro- meda polifolia, Narthecium ossifragum and Scirpus caespitosus. Predominant peat mosses are Sphagnum magellanicum, S. papillosum and S. rubellum.","collectionunitid":34873},"dataset":{"agerange":[{"units":"Calendar years BP","ageold":-46,"ageyoung":-46}],"database":"Neotoma Testate Amoebae Database","datasetid":48417,"datasetpi":[{"initials":"B.G.","contactid":105,"firstname":"Barry G.","familyname":"Warner","contactname":"Warner, Barry G."},{"initials":"T.E.","contactid":604,"firstname":"T. Edward","familyname":"Turner","contactname":"Turner, T. Edward"},{"initials":"R.J.","contactid":6543,"firstname":"Richard","familyname":"Payne","contactname":"Payne, Richard"},{"initials":"M.J.","contactid":7245,"firstname":"Matthew J.","familyname":"Amesbury","contactname":"Amesbury, Matthew J."},{"initials":"D.J.","contactid":7252,"firstname":"Daniel J.","familyname":"Charman","contactname":"Charman, Daniel J."},{"initials":"M.","contactid":7256,"firstname":"Michelle","familyname":"Garneau","contactname":"Garneau, Michelle"},{"initials":"P.D.M.","contactid":7260,"firstname":"Paul D. M.","familyname":"Hughes","contactname":"Hughes, Paul D. M."},{"initials":"M.","contactid":7267,"firstname":"Mariusz","familyname":"Lamentowicz","contactname":"Lamentowicz, Mariusz"},{"initials